  "about": "Raw measurements behind M5C.10e2 (docs/COVERAGE.md 'After batch 5' item 6, ADR-0033's M5C.10e2 amendment): how common is a request init that spreads a conditional of object literals after its method (fetch(url, { method, headers, ...(body ? { body: JSON.stringify(body) } : {}) })), which before the fix hid the method (any spread could supply it), so a wrapper's callers had no method and were AMBIGUOUS or matched every method. 'counts': GitHub REST GET /search/code (legacy engine, authenticated) total_count per query on 2026-11-06; the legacy engine drops punctuation, so the quoted phrases match token runs (body body JSON stringify body, fetch, method) and the counts only give scale. 'sample': the first 10 non-fork hits (one per repo) of each of the first two queries, each file read with GET /repos/<repo>/contents/<path>, saved, and analyzed alone as a one-file repo with the built analyzer (parsed, never run; eval/dist/usage-spreads-analyze.mjs). 'sites': fetch/axios calls whose init object literal (written at the call) spreads a conditional or &&; files with 0 build the init elsewhere (a variable) or in a helper the regex-free scan doesn't see. 'requests': requests the analyzer reports at those calls (a wrapper's callers each count). 'methodReadBefore': with this commit's analyzer but HEAD's values.ts and http.ts (packages/analyzer/dist/make-old-spread.mjs); 'methodReadAfter': with the fix. Of the 42 requests still without a method, 36 (724-office, Portfolio_Frontend, ha-home-energy-advisor) take method from a destructured options parameter with a default (async function api(path, { method = 'GET', body } = {})), a separate form this change doesn't touch. Among the eval checkouts (every repos.json entry, scanned for ...(x ? { / ...(x && { in files that request; eval/dist/spread-scan.mjs), the form in a request init is only in batch 5's solid-logic-studios/bucketwise-planner; the other hits spread into headers, message or request bodies, or Prisma queries, and batch 2's nemanjam/nextjs-prisma-boilerplate spreads ...(NODE_ENV !== 'test' && { onUploadProgress }) into an axios config whose method the call already fixes (its eval scores are unchanged).",
